<title>DUBAI: OPEC monitoring meeting in Iran due March 15-17.</title>
<headline>OPEC monitoring meeting in Iran due March 15-17.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>OPEC's ministerial monitoring committee is scheduled to meet March 15-17 on the Iranian island of Kish, an official at the National Iranian Oil Company (NIOC) in Tehran said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The committee, made up of ministers from Iran, Nigeria and Indonesia would review production &quot;violations&quot;, the source said.</p>
<p>OPEC pumped 26.64 million barrels per day (bpd) in January according to a Reuters survey, well above the group's agreed ceiling of 25.033 million bpd.</p>
<p>Venezuela remains the largest quota buster with its output reaching 3.17 million bpd last month compared to its quota of 2.359 million, according to independent assessments.</p>
<p>Iranian Oil Minister Gholamreza Aghazadeh on Sunday urged fellow OPEC states to abide by their quotas to reverse a slide in world oil prices.</p>
</text>
